WEBVTT

1
00:02:23.916 --> 00:02:26.919
<i>Duty is sacrifice.</i>

2
00:02:28.045 --> 00:02:32.133
<i>It eclipses all
things. even blood.</i>

3
00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:37.013
<i>All men of honor
must pay its price.</i>

4
00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:45.228
<i>The North owes a great
duty to the Seven Kingdoms.</i>

5
00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:48.481
<i>One older than any oath.</i>

6
00:02:48.482 --> 00:02:52.319
<i>Since the days of the First
Men. we have stood as guardians</i>

7
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.196
<i>against the cold and the dark.</i>

8
00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.449
<i>Through its long tradition.</i>

9
00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.286
<i>the Night's Watch cultivated
its strength from doomed men</i>

10
00:03:01.287 --> 00:03:03.955
<i>who had their life as
their only possession.</i>

11
00:03:03.956 --> 00:03:06.750
<i>But my ancestor. Torrhen Stark.</i>

12
00:03:06.751 --> 00:03:11.296
<i>began a tradition by making an
offering at the onset of winter:</i>

13
00:03:11.297 --> 00:03:16.636
<i>one in 10 men from our household was
to be chosen to fortify the Watch.</i>

14
00:03:19.513 --> 00:03:23.684
<i>This is not a
sentence but an honor.</i>

15
00:03:24.894 --> 00:03:28.939
<i>A duty embraced by all
who serve the North.</i>

16
00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.233
<i>Even by mine own kin.</i>

17
00:03:36.405 --> 00:03:38.824
<i>The North must stand ready.</i>

18
00:03:40.201 --> 00:03:41.785
<i>Winter is coming.</i>

19
00:03:41.786 --> 00:03:44.037
Coming? What is this. then.

20
00:03:44.038 --> 00:03:46.039
that falls from the skies
and shivers my bones?

21
00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.793
This is only a late
summer snow. my prince.

22
00:03:49.794 --> 00:03:52.295
In winter. it will
cover all you see.

23
00:03:52.296 --> 00:03:54.757
and all memories of
warmth will be forgotten.

24
00:03:55.883 --> 00:03:58.051
It pleases me to think
that over a century ago

25
00:03:58.052 --> 00:04:00.763
our ancestors treated
in this very place.

26
00:04:02.139 --> 00:04:04.100
The Conqueror and the
King in the North.

27
00:04:05.851 --> 00:04:09.981
You. at least. had the mercy not
to threaten me with your dragon.

28
00:04:18.197 --> 00:04:19.323
My prince.

29
00:04:20.116 --> 00:04:22.076
- My lord.
- My lord.

30
00:04:22.952 --> 00:04:24.202
M'lord.

31
00:04:24.203 --> 00:04:29.499
Surely the great Torrhen Stark would've
sooner died than bent the knee.

32
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:33.129
Unless he believed the Conqueror could
bring unity to the Seven Kingdoms.

33
00:04:34.422 --> 00:04:36.131
You are right in that.

34
00:04:36.132 --> 00:04:38.426
That unity is now threatened.

35
00:04:39.343 --> 00:04:41.928
The realm will soon
tear itself apart

36
00:04:41.929 --> 00:04:44.682
if men do not remember the
oath sworn to King Viserys

37
00:04:45.141 --> 00:04:47.309
and to his rightful heir.

38
00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.855
Starks do not forget
their oaths. my prince.

39
00:04:51.397 --> 00:04:56.152
But you must know that my gaze is
forever torn between north and south.

40
00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.614
In winter. my duty to the
Wall is even more dire

41
00:05:00.615 --> 00:05:02.366
than the one I owe
to King's Landing.

42
00:05:02.491 --> 00:05:04.659
I need my men here.

43
00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.662
Whilst your men guard against
wildlings and weather.

44
00:05:07.663 --> 00:05:10.333
the Hightowers plan
to usurp the throne.

45
00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.711
If my mother is to defend her
claim to hold the realm united.

46
00:05:14.712 --> 00:05:16.087
she needs an army.

47
00:05:16.088 --> 00:05:17.130
War is coming

48
00:05:17.131 --> 00:05:19.215
to the whole of
the realm. my lord.

49
00:05:19.216 --> 00:05:22.136
We cannot wage it without
the support of the North.

50
00:05:30.186 --> 00:05:34.440
My father brought King Jaehaerys
and Queen Alysanne to see the Wall.

51
00:05:35.149 --> 00:05:39.861
His Grace stood at this very outlook
and watched as their dragons.

52
00:05:39.862 --> 00:05:43.950
the greatest power in the
world. refused to cross it.

53
00:05:46.118 --> 00:05:49.955
Do you think my ancestors
built a 700-foot wall of ice

54
00:05:49.956 --> 00:05:52.458
to keep out snow and savages?

55
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:54.877
What does it keep out?

56
00:05:57.004 --> 00:05:58.339
Death.

57
00:06:06.347 --> 00:06:10.976
I have thousands of graybeards
who've already seen too many winters.

58
00:06:10.977 --> 00:06:14.354
They are well-honed.

59
00:06:14.355 --> 00:06:16.065
So they're old?

60
00:06:16.941 --> 00:06:19.734
I can ready them
to march at once.

61
00:06:19.735 --> 00:06:23.405
If your graybeards can fight.
the queen will have them.

62
00:06:23.406 --> 00:06:25.282
They will fight hard.

63
00:06:25.283 --> 00:06:27.075
Like Northerners.

64
00:06:27.076 --> 00:06:28.244
My lord?

65
00:06:29.954 --> 00:06:31.454
A raven's arrived.

66
00:06:31.455 --> 00:06:33.374
Urgent news from Dragonstone.

67
00:07:15.958 --> 00:07:19.337
Take your mount again.
We're flying out.

68
00:07:22.006 --> 00:07:25.550
I alone patrol over a
hundred miles of open sea.

69
00:07:25.551 --> 00:07:28.471
endlessly. to hold the blockade.

70
00:07:29.388 --> 00:07:32.892
Meleys must gorge
and rest. as must I.

71
00:07:34.393 --> 00:07:36.853
- We're going to King's Landing.
- To what end?

72
00:07:36.854 --> 00:07:41.483
Killing Vhagar. I cannot face
that hoary old bitch alone.

73
00:07:41.484 --> 00:07:45.654
With my dragon and yours together.
we can kill Vhagar and her rider.

74
00:07:45.655 --> 00:07:47.031
Make it a son for a son.

75
00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:51.993
- Was this the queen's command?
- The queen remains absent.

76
00:07:51.994 --> 00:07:54.037
I should be at
Harrenhal bending knees.

77
00:07:54.038 --> 00:07:56.748
but I must instead remain
here to wage her war.

78
00:07:56.749 --> 00:07:59.417
Or perhaps. more simply.
to await her return.

79
00:07:59.418 --> 00:08:02.796
She has been gone for days.
Too long. She is exposed.

80
00:08:02.797 --> 00:08:05.090
- She is grieving.
- The mother grieves

81
00:08:05.091 --> 00:08:07.551
as the queen shirks her duties.

82
00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.765
It was a raven that brought
me news of Laena's death.

83
00:08:13.766 --> 00:08:15.935
I existed for weeks in torment

84
00:08:17.019 --> 00:08:19.939
refusing to believe
what I'd been told.

85
00:08:21.941 --> 00:08:24.651
It was only when I saw my
daughter's mortal remains

86
00:08:24.652 --> 00:08:27.154
that I could begin to mourn her.

87
00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:33.119
A raven has told Rhaenyra
that her son is dead.

88
00:08:34.287 --> 00:08:35.745
She needs to know
it for certain.

89
00:08:35.746 --> 00:08:37.832
She was a fool to go alone.

90
00:08:38.624 --> 00:08:40.208
What if Aemond were
to happen upon her?

91
00:08:40.209 --> 00:08:42.086
Then I would pity Aemond.

92
00:08:44.714 --> 00:08:46.882
The queen was wise
to recuse herself.

93
00:08:48.009 --> 00:08:52.054
She has not acted on the vengeful
impulse that others might have.

94
00:08:53.431 --> 00:08:56.558
If you'd have acted
when you had the chance.

95
00:08:56.559 --> 00:08:58.686
Aegon's line would
be extinguished.

96
00:09:00.605 --> 00:09:02.440
And Luke would be alive.

97
00:09:10.031 --> 00:09:11.657
Fly with me.

98
00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:15.995
- It is a command.
- Would that you were the king.

99
00:10:25.856 --> 00:10:26.983
M'lord.

100
00:10:29.777 --> 00:10:33.030
It's a marvel she was able to
return from the Stepstones at all.

101
00:10:35.408 --> 00:10:37.201
Barely done. but done.

102
00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:41.371
Seven more ships put out to sea
this morn' to fortify the blockade.

103
00:10:41.372 --> 00:10:43.790
The Gullet is vast. and we're
not like to have the numbers

104
00:10:43.791 --> 00:10:46.085
to cover all that open water.

105
00:10:48.796 --> 00:10:51.965
I must have my ship back
at sea to lead the effort.

106
00:10:51.966 --> 00:10:54.594
It'll be many weeks
yet. I'd wager.

107
00:10:56.512 --> 00:10:57.972
But I'll have a
word with my brother

108
00:10:59.015 --> 00:11:02.226
to see what reinforcements
the shipwrights can muster.

109
00:11:12.153 --> 00:11:14.739
The smithy delivered
this earlier.

110
00:11:16.991 --> 00:11:18.200
M'lord?

111
00:11:26.876 --> 00:11:29.879
I had this commissioned
for Prince Lucerys.

112
00:11:32.173 --> 00:11:35.134
I was very sorry to hear
about your heir's death.

113
00:11:35.676 --> 00:11:37.678
'Twas the blackest
of treacheries.

114
00:11:40.973 --> 00:11:45.019
Pardon. m'lord. if it'll
please you. much to do.

115
00:11:45.853 --> 00:11:49.190
They tell me that you are the one
that dragged my body out of the sea.

116
00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.197
It was only my duty.

117
00:12:00.743 --> 00:12:03.871
I am indebted to you. Alyn.

118
00:12:43.452 --> 00:12:45.079
Mind your posts!

119
00:12:47.999 --> 00:12:50.001
Keep your focus. men!

120
00:12:53.588 --> 00:12:56.047
- Dragon!
- Dragon!

121
00:12:56.048 --> 00:12:57.466
Arm the scorpion!

122
00:12:57.758 --> 00:12:59.969
Arm the scorpion!

123
00:13:01.846 --> 00:13:04.180
Approaching from the southeast!

124
00:13:04.181 --> 00:13:05.474
Get around!

125
00:13:09.979 --> 00:13:11.563
Scorpion ready!

126
00:13:11.564 --> 00:13:13.941
- Halt!
- Halt!

127
00:13:16.736 --> 00:13:18.112
Stand down. it's Vhagar!

128
00:13:18.821 --> 00:13:20.030
Stand down!

129
00:13:20.031 --> 00:13:21.949
Standing down!

130
00:13:48.851 --> 00:13:50.603
Where is Jaehaerys?

131
00:13:52.021 --> 00:13:54.023
Attending his lessons.

132
00:13:54.815 --> 00:13:56.524
And those are where?

133
00:13:56.525 --> 00:13:58.026
What do you need of him?

134
00:13:58.027 --> 00:14:00.195
Taking him to the small council.

135
00:14:00.196 --> 00:14:03.199
He'll be king one day. He
must begin his instruction.

136
00:14:03.616 --> 00:14:05.826
What if he does not
want to be king?

137
00:14:06.994 --> 00:14:08.286
Where is he?

138
00:14:08.287 --> 00:14:09.455
The library.

139
00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.291
You must not
interrupt his custom.

140
00:14:19.048 --> 00:14:20.716
I'm afraid.

141
00:14:23.177 --> 00:14:24.387
Don't be.

142
00:14:25.096 --> 00:14:27.431
They'd be fools to come with
Vhagar protecting the city.

143
00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:29.892
Not the dragons.

144
00:14:30.768 --> 00:14:31.978
The rats.

145
00:14:40.987 --> 00:14:43.406
The queen is an
enduring mystery.

146
00:14:44.156 --> 00:14:45.574
is she not?

147
00:15:19.442 --> 00:15:21.110
There's a chill in the air.

148
00:15:25.489 --> 00:15:27.700
Summer is well
and truly through.

149
00:15:29.201 --> 00:15:32.038
We are expected at the
small council. Your Grace.

150
00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:49.138
We cannot.

151
00:15:49.847 --> 00:15:51.057
Again.

152
00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.686
Yes. Your Grace.

153
00:16:00.399 --> 00:16:02.401
If you wouldn't mind?

154
00:16:35.434 --> 00:16:37.228
- Your Grace.
- Good day.

155
00:16:42.233 --> 00:16:44.526
Hello! Jaehaerys must
learn the ways of the court

156
00:16:44.527 --> 00:16:46.569
if he is to rule one day.

157
00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:47.863
Up we go.

158
00:16:49.824 --> 00:16:52.200
Good morrow. my lords.

159
00:16:52.201 --> 00:16:53.286
Mother.

160
00:16:55.454 --> 00:16:57.247
What news?

161
00:16:57.248 --> 00:17:01.961
Our letters to the Vale and to the
North continue to go unanswered.

162
00:17:02.628 --> 00:17:03.629
Cunts.

163
00:17:05.298 --> 00:17:09.302
The Stormlands should be ours
after Prince Aemond's marriage pact

164
00:17:09.427 --> 00:17:11.595
to the Lady Floris Baratheon.

165
00:17:11.596 --> 00:17:13.806
I anticipate their
sworn declaration.

166
00:17:14.765 --> 00:17:17.892
My brother is raising
the strength of the West

167
00:17:17.893 --> 00:17:21.021
to mass at the Golden
Tooth. but we...

168
00:17:21.022 --> 00:17:25.108
Yeah. thank you. my prince.
That's very helpful.

169
00:17:25.109 --> 00:17:26.651
My nephew. Lord Ormund.

170
00:17:26.652 --> 00:17:29.904
musters his forces to
sally forth from Oldtown.

171
00:17:29.905 --> 00:17:31.448
They expect to march quickly.

172
00:17:31.449 --> 00:17:34.951
meeting little resistance.
until they reach the Riverlands.

173
00:17:34.952 --> 00:17:36.912
My letters to Rhaenyra.
Has there been any answer?

174
00:17:36.996 --> 00:17:39.623
An apology for her dead son?

175
00:17:39.624 --> 00:17:41.166
None. Your Grace.

176
00:17:41.167 --> 00:17:43.418
Between that and their
blockade of the Gullet.

177
00:17:43.419 --> 00:17:45.462
we must presume that
the princess has refused

178
00:17:45.463 --> 00:17:46.964
the offered terms

179
00:17:47.089 --> 00:17:49.591
and that war is now inevitable.

180
00:17:49.592 --> 00:17:51.593
Perhaps Your Grace might lend

181
00:17:51.594 --> 00:17:53.930
- his voice to our outreach...
- Stop! Enough!

182
00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.016
in hopes that new terms
might be negotiated.

183
00:17:57.141 --> 00:17:59.935
Release it at once!
Would someone please?

184
00:17:59.936 --> 00:18:02.855
Is the heir to the throne
bothering you. Tyland?

185
00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:08.026
No. No. no. not in
the least. Your Grace.

186
00:18:08.027 --> 00:18:10.487
Because I think he wants a ride.

187
00:18:10.488 --> 00:18:11.738
- Your Grace.
- A ride?

188
00:18:11.739 --> 00:18:13.240
A pony ride.

189
00:18:13.366 --> 00:18:14.908
Wouldn't that be fun. Jaehaerys?

190
00:18:14.909 --> 00:18:17.411
Should the Master of
Coin be your royal steed?

191
00:18:26.587 --> 00:18:28.005
Your Grace!

192
00:18:28.923 --> 00:18:31.050
There are important
matters to discuss

193
00:18:32.551 --> 00:18:34.303
despite Sir Tyland's
interruptions.

194
00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.265
Very well.

195
00:18:38.099 --> 00:18:40.518
No time for amusements. Tyland.

196
00:18:41.936 --> 00:18:43.145
Your Grace.

197
00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:46.649
Off you go. Jaehaerys. Good boy.

198
00:18:49.151 --> 00:18:50.695
Where were we?

199
00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:56.449
Rhaenyra's blockade has placed
King's Landing under strain.

200
00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.827
And those pressures
will multiply quickly.

201
00:18:58.828 --> 00:19:00.870
Well. we should've just killed
her when we had the chance.

202
00:19:00.871 --> 00:19:04.582
Regrettably. the opportunity
for surprise has been lost

203
00:19:04.583 --> 00:19:08.337
and. with it. the chance to
end this conflict quickly.

204
00:19:09.714 --> 00:19:11.756
We must play the
board before us.

205
00:19:11.757 --> 00:19:14.426
If we are to break the
Sea Snake's blockade.

206
00:19:14.427 --> 00:19:17.096
we will need to bolster both the
Lannister and Hightower navies.

207
00:19:17.221 --> 00:19:19.849
We do have need for a
new Master of Ships.

208
00:19:20.558 --> 00:19:23.184
We could offer the title to
the young Lord Dalton Greyjoy.

209
00:19:23.185 --> 00:19:25.395
Aemond. What is
your business here?

210
00:19:25.396 --> 00:19:26.646
The king summoned me.

211
00:19:26.647 --> 00:19:28.440
You do not have a
seat at this council.

212
00:19:28.441 --> 00:19:31.735
Aemond is my closest
blood and our best sword.

213
00:19:31.736 --> 00:19:33.237
I welcome him.

214
00:19:33.946 --> 00:19:36.906
Path to King's Landing is
through the Riverlands.

215
00:19:36.907 --> 00:19:40.577
We must establish a toehold
there. at Harrenhal.

216
00:19:40.578 --> 00:19:42.579
The Riverlords will
either declare for me

217
00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.624
or they will meet Vhagar
and Sunfyre together.

218
00:19:45.625 --> 00:19:47.959
And we can burn the
blockade while we're at it.

219
00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.920
- Rhaenyra has dragons as well.
- Mine are bigger.

220
00:19:49.921 --> 00:19:52.380
If we lose the dragons to war.
there'll be no calling them back.

221
00:19:52.381 --> 00:19:54.007
- We must proceed cautiously.
- No.

222
00:19:54.008 --> 00:19:58.095
Fat. old Lord Tully will either
raise my banner or see his burn.

223
00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:00.181
We should fly to Riverrun.

224
00:20:00.723 --> 00:20:03.808
You are the king. Your Grace. You
must not put yourself at risk.

225
00:20:03.809 --> 00:20:06.561
And Vhagar is needed here to
deter Rhaenyra from attacking

226
00:20:06.562 --> 00:20:09.190
in retribution for
the death of her son.

227
00:20:10.316 --> 00:20:14.611
Errors were made in the hours
following King Viserys's death.

228
00:20:14.612 --> 00:20:16.238
We mustn't compound them.

229
00:20:18.491 --> 00:20:21.076
You've already demonstrated
your might. Your Grace.

230
00:20:21.077 --> 00:20:25.372
We must now favor
patience and restraint.

231
00:20:25.373 --> 00:20:27.207
I send ravens by the hour.

232
00:20:27.208 --> 00:20:31.586
Many and more houses will
declare for you in time.

233
00:20:31.587 --> 00:20:34.799
History and precedent
will come to your side.

234
00:20:42.598 --> 00:20:43.765
Good morrow. Your Grace.

235
00:20:43.766 --> 00:20:45.434
Good morrow. Lord Larys.

236
00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:49.187
I had come earlier to have a word
before the small council convened.

237
00:20:49.188 --> 00:20:53.776
but your handmaiden said
that you were indisposed.

238
00:20:57.029 --> 00:20:59.073
What is it you wish to discuss?

239
00:21:01.117 --> 00:21:04.537
I have completed questioning
the whole of the castle staff.

240
00:21:05.705 --> 00:21:07.497
They produced rather
interesting details

241
00:21:07.498 --> 00:21:10.960
but I am satisfied I have exposed
all who betrayed our trust.

242
00:21:14.046 --> 00:21:15.172
And what of them?

243
00:21:16.716 --> 00:21:18.926
They no longer breathe our air.

244
00:21:21.095 --> 00:21:23.931
I have chosen your
new staff personally.

245
00:21:43.117 --> 00:21:45.410
Give me that.

246
00:21:45.411 --> 00:21:46.746
Your Grace?

247
00:21:47.413 --> 00:21:49.415
Just leave me.

248
00:21:51.083 --> 00:21:53.127
Just leave me.

249
00:22:35.962 --> 00:22:38.130
- It's a dragon wing!
- Let's have a look!

250
00:22:39.757 --> 00:22:41.759
- It's a wing.
- Who cares what it is.

251
00:22:42.677 --> 00:22:44.303
Dragon!

252
00:24:11.015 --> 00:24:14.184
All hail King Aegon!

253
00:24:14.185 --> 00:24:16.645
"Aegon the Magnanimous."

254
00:24:16.646 --> 00:24:21.733
Second of His Name. King of the Andals.
and the Rhoynar. and the First Men.

255
00:24:21.734 --> 00:24:24.986
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.
and Protector of the Realm.

256
00:24:24.987 --> 00:24:27.073
Hail King Aegon!

257
00:24:27.782 --> 00:24:29.408
"The Magnanimous"?

258
00:24:33.120 --> 00:24:34.330
Your Grace.

259
00:24:34.956 --> 00:24:38.000
Let's have the first
petition. my good Lord Hand.

260
00:24:42.421 --> 00:24:44.214
Good morrow. my... Your Grace.

261
00:24:44.215 --> 00:24:47.676
It's alright. There's
no reason to be nervous.

262
00:24:47.677 --> 00:24:48.843
What's your name?

263
00:24:48.844 --> 00:24:51.096
Gr... Jerard. Your Grace.

264
00:24:51.097 --> 00:24:55.393
Good morrow. Jerard. And how
might your king be of service?

265
00:24:55.893 --> 00:24:57.561
'Tis my flock.

266
00:24:58.562 --> 00:25:02.191
A tenth of them taken by

267
00:25:04.193 --> 00:25:09.322
the Crown on. on
the cusp of winter.

268
00:25:09.323 --> 00:25:12.368
- If I'd had the time to plan...
- We should return them.

269
00:25:15.454 --> 00:25:16.913
Your Grace?

270
00:25:16.914 --> 00:25:18.540
Well. you need your goats
for the winter. don't you?

271
00:25:18.541 --> 00:25:21.376
- Sheep. Your Grace.
- Sheep. even better.

272
00:25:21.377 --> 00:25:23.796
I shall make your
flock of sheep whole.

273
00:25:25.631 --> 00:25:28.049
We already made a promise
to all the Crownlands

274
00:25:28.050 --> 00:25:32.721
that a tithing of livestock would
be necessary to sustain the dragons

275
00:25:32.722 --> 00:25:37.268
for their increased activity
and. pray not. eventual fighting.

276
00:25:37.935 --> 00:25:39.978
Right. Right.

277
00:25:39.979 --> 00:25:43.023
Perhaps we could just return
his sheep. He came all this way.

278
00:25:43.024 --> 00:25:45.692
If you return one herder's
sheep. Your Grace.

279
00:25:45.693 --> 00:25:48.111
you will soon find them all
at the foot of your throne

280
00:25:48.112 --> 00:25:50.031
expecting the same.

281
00:25:50.573 --> 00:25:52.032
They won't know.

282
00:25:52.033 --> 00:25:58.033
When the king speaks.
Your Grace. all hear it.

283
00:26:06.923 --> 00:26:12.302
After further thought. I have decided
that I cannot restore your sheep.

284
00:26:12.303 --> 00:26:15.513
If war were to break out. my
dragons will require feed.

285
00:26:15.514 --> 00:26:17.016
Bring the next.

286
00:26:18.434 --> 00:26:22.020
Salts always run scarce
on the road to winter.

287
00:26:22.021 --> 00:26:23.063
Your Grace.

288
00:26:23.064 --> 00:26:26.483
We rely on ships from
Essos for our supply.

289
00:26:26.484 --> 00:26:29.736
But now. with a blockade in
place and war threatening...

290
00:26:29.737 --> 00:26:31.780
Yeah. that treasonous
blockade won't last long.

291
00:26:31.781 --> 00:26:34.324
I plan to send Vhagar
to burn it to ash.

292
00:26:34.325 --> 00:26:35.660
Bring the next.

293
00:26:39.705 --> 00:26:41.332
Hugh. Your Grace.

294
00:26:44.794 --> 00:26:48.547
The smiths are all proud to support
Your Grace against Rhaenyra.

295
00:26:52.301 --> 00:26:53.261
But?

296
00:26:53.262 --> 00:26:54.553
But...

297
00:26:56.264 --> 00:26:58.266
iron costs have grown.

298
00:26:59.183 --> 00:27:02.603
A lone scorpion
takes weeks to build.

299
00:27:03.396 --> 00:27:05.064
To put it simply.
we are struggling.

300
00:27:06.440 --> 00:27:10.860
If we could but have the Crown's
coin before we started work.

301
00:27:10.861 --> 00:27:12.862
it would bring great relief.

302
00:27:12.863 --> 00:27:16.242
Not just to me. but to all
the smiths serving your cause.

303
00:27:20.830 --> 00:27:23.374
You shall be paid and paid well.

304
00:27:24.292 --> 00:27:26.501
My army cannot win a war
without your weapons.

305
00:27:26.502 --> 00:27:28.546
You should continue
their making.

306
00:27:28.963 --> 00:27:32.758
Our victory depends on the
efforts of the smallfolk.

307
00:27:35.177 --> 00:27:37.430
You have my most sincere
gratitude. Your Grace.

308
00:27:38.347 --> 00:27:40.349
I'll hear the next petition.

309
00:27:47.940 --> 00:27:50.776
Your Grace. it filled my heart
to see you on the Iron Throne.

310
00:27:51.485 --> 00:27:53.987
I was only a boy when
Jaehaerys last graced the seat.

311
00:27:53.988 --> 00:27:55.447
but you brought forth
memories of him.

312
00:27:55.448 --> 00:27:57.574
and you have such a deft
touch with the smallfolk.

313
00:27:57.575 --> 00:27:59.409
just as your father did.

314
00:27:59.410 --> 00:28:00.911
Thank you. my lord.

315
00:28:01.412 --> 00:28:03.623
I wonder. do you have a
moment for a quiet word?

316
00:28:09.712 --> 00:28:13.049
It is the Hand's wont to
keep a firm grip on things.

317
00:28:15.343 --> 00:28:17.261
He controlled your
father the same way.

318
00:28:19.013 --> 00:28:21.598
Viserys had a certain
reputation as being pliable.

319
00:28:21.599 --> 00:28:23.100
I am aware.

320
00:28:24.769 --> 00:28:27.062
I would think. as
we find ourselves

321
00:28:27.063 --> 00:28:29.314
standing within a
hair's breadth of war.

322
00:28:29.315 --> 00:28:32.193
that you would wish to
be viewed differently.

323
00:28:35.529 --> 00:28:36.863
How?

324
00:28:36.864 --> 00:28:38.616
Otto Hightower

325
00:28:40.034 --> 00:28:42.954
was your father's
Hand. Your Grace.

326
00:28:59.595 --> 00:29:00.805
Daughter.

327
00:29:02.014 --> 00:29:04.642
I requested an
audience hours ago.

328
00:29:05.935 --> 00:29:09.772
There were many petitions.

329
00:29:12.441 --> 00:29:14.277
I find myself wondering.

330
00:29:15.444 --> 00:29:17.238
do we pursue the same end?

331
00:29:19.323 --> 00:29:22.743
I must admit. there are days
where I myself can't be sure.

332
00:29:24.495 --> 00:29:26.497
I shall tell you mine.

333
00:29:28.124 --> 00:29:29.582
It's victory.

334
00:29:29.583 --> 00:29:32.419
And how would you
define "victory"?

335
00:29:32.420 --> 00:29:34.379
Rhaenyra bending the knee

336
00:29:34.380 --> 00:29:37.049
and Aegon sitting the
Iron Throne. in peace.

337
00:29:37.842 --> 00:29:39.301
As Viserys wished.

338
00:29:39.302 --> 00:29:42.971
Well. if that's how you describe
it. then we are aligned.

339
00:29:42.972 --> 00:29:45.098
- Then be my ally.
- I am.

340
00:29:45.099 --> 00:29:48.935
An ally would not repeatedly cut my legs
from beneath me at that table of men!

341
00:29:48.936 --> 00:29:52.606
- I sit there and I feel your anger.
- Frustration.

342
00:29:52.607 --> 00:29:55.066
These critical days
since Viserys's passing

343
00:29:55.067 --> 00:29:57.987
- haven't gone to plan.
- That's not my fault.

344
00:29:59.530 --> 00:30:02.033
My sons both see you
as the great example.

345
00:30:02.575 --> 00:30:03.743
The Hand to three kings.

346
00:30:05.494 --> 00:30:08.789
Aegon is ever-eager to
prove himself and Aemond...

347
00:30:10.416 --> 00:30:12.043
Aemond is angry.

348
00:30:13.586 --> 00:30:16.171
Rhaenyra's son took his eye
and was never punished for it.

349
00:30:16.172 --> 00:30:20.301
- What he did. however vicious...
- The caprice of youth.

350
00:30:24.931 --> 00:30:26.723
I could only hope.

351
00:30:26.724 --> 00:30:28.893
Aemond erred.

352
00:30:29.977 --> 00:30:33.396
But he is fiercely loyal.
He wishes to please.

353
00:30:33.397 --> 00:30:36.734
And Aegon still heeds
me. In private. at least.

354
00:30:38.277 --> 00:30:41.530
But if you undermine my voice. both
those boys will grow deaf to it.

355
00:30:49.956 --> 00:30:51.832
I hadn't seen it that way.

356
00:30:52.416 --> 00:30:56.671
We only need to mind Aegon until
the novelty of rule is spent.

357
00:30:57.588 --> 00:31:00.674
Once he tires of it. you and I
can steer our cause to victory.

358
00:31:00.675 --> 00:31:03.386
A fine strategy. daughter.

359
00:31:04.053 --> 00:31:09.684
But you must accept that the path
to victory now is one of violence.

360
00:31:10.685 --> 00:31:12.311
I know it.

361
00:31:16.065 --> 00:31:18.276
But that does not mean
it must be wanton.

362
00:31:20.611 --> 00:31:21.612
No.

363
00:31:38.421 --> 00:31:40.673
Prepare to be boarded!

364
00:31:43.301 --> 00:31:46.428
By the order of Lord
Corlys Velaryon!

365
00:31:46.429 --> 00:31:49.140
Search the hold for stowaways!

366
00:32:16.709 --> 00:32:17.710
You.

367
00:32:20.254 --> 00:32:23.466
When last we met.
there were two of you.

368
00:32:25.718 --> 00:32:27.177
"The White Worm."

369
00:32:27.178 --> 00:32:29.763
Did you think I would
wither in your absence?

370
00:32:29.764 --> 00:32:31.806
I did not think you
would flower a traitor.

371
00:32:31.807 --> 00:32:35.143
You speak of highborn
games. I am common-born.

372
00:32:35.144 --> 00:32:37.646
How long have you been selling
secrets to Otto Hightower?

373
00:32:37.647 --> 00:32:39.482
As long as he had
gold to pay for them.

374
00:32:42.109 --> 00:32:46.322
Who sent you fleeing from King's
Landing in such disrepair. hm?

375
00:32:47.865 --> 00:32:49.824
You put Aegon on the throne.

376
00:32:49.825 --> 00:32:51.952
That was the
Hightowers' conspiracy.

377
00:32:51.953 --> 00:32:54.496
I merely profited from
knowing Aegon's movements.

378
00:32:54.497 --> 00:32:56.081
But you delivered him.

379
00:32:56.082 --> 00:32:59.000
He would've returned home
eventually for gold and for respite.

380
00:32:59.001 --> 00:33:00.168
as he always does.

381
00:33:00.169 --> 00:33:03.296
I simply. simply sped
the business along.

382
00:33:03.297 --> 00:33:05.340
"Business" that ended with the
theft of the queen's throne

383
00:33:05.341 --> 00:33:06.591
and the murder of her son.

384
00:33:06.592 --> 00:33:08.551
You only blame me
because your true enemies

385
00:33:08.552 --> 00:33:10.263
are out of reach.

386
00:33:11.806 --> 00:33:14.766
My arrangement with the Hand
was purely transactional.

387
00:33:14.767 --> 00:33:16.769
I held no loyalty to him.

388
00:33:17.478 --> 00:33:19.397
Certainly do not now.

389
00:33:19.981 --> 00:33:23.108
Otto Hightower was to me
as I am to your noble ilk.

390
00:33:23.109 --> 00:33:24.693
fodder to be cast off.

391
00:33:24.694 --> 00:33:26.361
What else do you know
of him? His plans?

392
00:33:26.362 --> 00:33:28.072
Little and less.

393
00:33:31.284 --> 00:33:34.495
I possess nothing of
value to you. Daemon.

394
00:33:57.518 --> 00:33:58.977
Have her moved to the cells.

395
00:33:58.978 --> 00:34:01.689
She is to be treated as
a traitor to the crown.

396
00:34:04.442 --> 00:34:08.028
Forgive me. my prince. but
the lady speaks the truth.

397
00:34:08.029 --> 00:34:10.823
- She was no agent of the Hightowers.
- What is it to you?

398
00:34:11.907 --> 00:34:14.367
- A matter of honor.
- Was it honor that made you stand by

399
00:34:14.368 --> 00:34:17.329
and watch as the Hightowers
usurped the throne?

400
00:34:17.330 --> 00:34:19.248
You and your traitorous twin.

401
00:34:19.957 --> 00:34:21.959
No. my prince.

402
00:34:23.336 --> 00:34:24.754
I'm shamed by it.

403
00:34:25.379 --> 00:34:29.507
That's why I abandoned the Kingsguard.
and my brother. and came here.

404
00:34:29.508 --> 00:34:31.218
I don't care.

405
00:34:32.094 --> 00:34:34.971
Aegon was in your grasp. You
should've killed him yourself.

406
00:34:34.972 --> 00:34:37.642
Arryk and I were named to the
Kingsguard at just 8 and 10.

407
00:34:38.601 --> 00:34:42.605
And we swore the same oath: to
defend the whole of the royal family.

408
00:34:44.315 --> 00:34:47.318
So what were we to do when they
turned against one another?

409
00:35:16.222 --> 00:35:20.517
Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen.
the First of Her Name.

410
00:35:20.518 --> 00:35:24.896
Queen of the Andals. and the
Rhoynar. and the First Men.

411
00:35:24.897 --> 00:35:28.985
Lady of the Seven Kingdoms.
and Protector of the Realm.

412
00:35:35.032 --> 00:35:37.243
Did you find what you needed?

413
00:35:45.835 --> 00:35:48.462
Your council stands at
the ready. Your Grace.

414
00:35:52.633 --> 00:35:57.096
I will fly to Harrenhal at your command
and set our toehold in the Riverlands.

415
00:35:58.097 --> 00:36:00.265
Your Grace. my lord husband's
blockade of the Gullet

416
00:36:00.266 --> 00:36:01.308
moves into place.

417
00:36:01.309 --> 00:36:04.854
All seaborne travel and trade to
King's Landing will soon be cut off.

418
00:36:10.901 --> 00:36:14.113
I want Aemond Targaryen.

419
00:37:02.536 --> 00:37:05.246
In your years as a
merchant of gossip.

420
00:37:05.247 --> 00:37:07.832
you surely accumulated
spies within the Red Keep.

421
00:37:07.833 --> 00:37:10.085
Servants who knew the
comings and goings.

422
00:37:10.086 --> 00:37:12.254
Scheme with someone
else. Daemon.

423
00:37:12.255 --> 00:37:15.549
I was once in your
thrall. but no longer.

424
00:37:16.592 --> 00:37:18.427
A transaction. then.

425
00:37:19.178 --> 00:37:22.390
Your knowledge in
exchange for your freedom.

426
00:37:49.709 --> 00:37:50.918
Your Grace.

427
00:37:54.672 --> 00:37:58.258
Lady Jeyne Arryn has
pledged her support

428
00:37:58.259 --> 00:38:01.262
in exchange for a dragon
to guard the Vale.

429
00:38:04.015 --> 00:38:07.018
And Lord Cregan Stark

430
00:38:09.895 --> 00:38:12.732
has promised 2.000 men...

431
00:38:58.110 --> 00:38:59.737
Alyrie Florent.

432
00:39:29.809 --> 00:39:31.811
Viserys Targaryen.

433
00:40:29.952 --> 00:40:31.454
Lucerys Velaryon.

434
00:41:26.217 --> 00:41:27.426
A tribute.

435
00:41:36.227 --> 00:41:37.811
Commander?

436
00:41:37.812 --> 00:41:39.897
Never gone for long.

437
00:41:41.691 --> 00:41:44.777
I'm told you bear a
mislike for the Hightowers.

438
00:41:46.195 --> 00:41:48.072
Fuck the Hightowers.

439
00:41:53.744 --> 00:41:55.371
Keep walking.

440
00:41:59.166 --> 00:42:01.168
Don't make trouble.

441
00:42:09.051 --> 00:42:12.512
The White Worm said you're
one of Aegon's ratcatchers.

442
00:42:12.513 --> 00:42:14.014
You must be busy.

443
00:42:14.015 --> 00:42:16.267
That castle positively
crawls with them now.

444
00:42:17.643 --> 00:42:19.603
I heard the White
Worm were dead.

445
00:42:19.604 --> 00:42:21.771
Her ghost told me you
were a betting man.

446
00:42:21.772 --> 00:42:22.939
Fighting pits?

447
00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:26.485
Dogs. and bones.

448
00:42:27.236 --> 00:42:28.988
How deep are your debts?

449
00:42:36.454 --> 00:42:38.246
I was also given to
understand that you possess

450
00:42:38.247 --> 00:42:40.332
a unique knowledge
of the Red Keep.

451
00:42:40.333 --> 00:42:42.459
Maegor's tunnels.

452
00:42:42.460 --> 00:42:44.462
Great big rat's nest. it is.

453
00:42:45.588 --> 00:42:48.716
I know them better than
the shape of my own cock.

454
00:42:51.260 --> 00:42:52.470
This is my friend.

455
00:42:53.804 --> 00:42:56.223
Tonight. he's going
to be your friend.

456
00:42:57.016 --> 00:43:00.019
You're to find and slay the
Prince Aemond Targaryen.

457
00:43:01.312 --> 00:43:03.813
He has silver hair and one eye.

458
00:43:03.814 --> 00:43:05.650
Should be easy enough to find.

459
00:43:07.985 --> 00:43:09.569
But I understand he's
quite good in a fight.

460
00:43:09.570 --> 00:43:11.489
You'll want to take caution.

461
00:43:13.115 --> 00:43:16.243
That's one half. You'll get
the other when it's done.

462
00:43:28.631 --> 00:43:29.840
Alright.

463
00:43:32.009 --> 00:43:33.761
What if we can't find him?

464
00:43:38.266 --> 00:43:41.810
We've wasted precious days in
this war of quills and ravens.

465
00:43:41.811 --> 00:43:43.896
Words are wind.

466
00:43:44.772 --> 00:43:47.065
You should be leading the van

467
00:43:47.066 --> 00:43:49.651
and I should be flying
cover on Vhagar.

468
00:43:49.652 --> 00:43:53.113
No castle would dare to raise
Rhaenyra's banner against us.

469
00:43:53.114 --> 00:43:56.157
We would bring the whole of the
Crownlands to heel in weeks.

470
00:43:56.158 --> 00:43:59.035
Well. mayhaps we could
petition the king.

471
00:43:59.036 --> 00:44:02.123
privately. to send us out.

472
00:44:03.916 --> 00:44:05.834
Rosby and Stokeworth.

473
00:44:05.835 --> 00:44:09.212
small castles right in the
shadow of King's Landing.

474
00:44:09.213 --> 00:44:10.797
They would not want
us for enemies.

475
00:44:10.798 --> 00:44:13.009
We could add their
levies to our own.

476
00:44:14.343 --> 00:44:16.804
Our host growing as we advance.

477
00:44:19.348 --> 00:44:21.350
It is a canny scheme.

478
00:44:21.976 --> 00:44:23.560
But moot.

479
00:44:23.561 --> 00:44:26.605
My brother is hostage to
my grandsire and mother

480
00:44:26.606 --> 00:44:30.150
and they tell him that a war
of dragons can yet be avoided.

481
00:44:30.151 --> 00:44:33.361
'Tis inevitable.
They must see that.

482
00:44:33.362 --> 00:44:35.615
Otto fears to upset
the order of things.

483
00:44:36.907 --> 00:44:38.909
And Alicent is simply...

484
00:44:40.119 --> 00:44:41.370
angry.

485
00:44:42.413 --> 00:44:45.874
- Angry?
- She blames me for starting this war

486
00:44:45.875 --> 00:44:49.962
after she plotted with my father's
council to usurp his throne.

487
00:44:51.756 --> 00:44:54.967
"Her Grace" speaks
with two tongues.

488
00:44:58.804 --> 00:45:01.057
She has a gentle heart.

489
00:45:01.682 --> 00:45:04.310
And Rhaenyra is
a cunning spider.

490
00:45:04.769 --> 00:45:08.730
Long ago. she drew
Alicent into her web.

491
00:45:08.731 --> 00:45:10.650
intoxicated her.

492
00:45:12.193 --> 00:45:13.486
It is not your mother's fault.

493
00:45:15.613 --> 00:45:17.823
She holds love for our enemy.

494
00:45:19.700 --> 00:45:21.702
That makes her a fool.

495
00:45:38.302 --> 00:45:39.512
Lord Hand.

496
